= Pins and themes

One selection per match, edited at once: the Helix way.

== Challenge 5

Make Musubi yours:

+ *Pin* this note: right click its row in the explorer (`Space e` shows or
  hides it) and choose _Pin_, or type `Space ?` and "pin". It appears under
  _Pinned_, on every copy of your vault. The four notes modified last are
  under _Recent_, and every note under _Notebook_.
+ Open the *settings* with `Space ,` and try the *Ayu Mirage* or *GitHub
  Dark* theme with the arrows. Keep it, or go back to _Follow the system_. Autosave is there
  too.
+ *Split* the window with `Space w v`: two panes, `Space w w` moves between
  them, `Space w q` closes one.

The next step is in the *graph* of the links: press `Space g`, find the note
named _Writing Typst_, click it to select it, then double click it (or
press `Enter`) to open it. `Space g` again leaves the graph.

The panel in its corner chooses what it shows: _All_ the notes, the notes
_Linked_ to the selected note (or the note of the pane) both ways, or the
notes of a _Folder_ you pick, with its subfolders. It draws the notes as
dots or as pills with their title inside, and can group the notes by
folder: each folder is a circle of its color, with the circles of its
subfolders inside. Notes
take the color of their folder: while the graph is shown, a dot of that
color follows each folder in the explorer.

